// ============================================================
// SKILL: Anti-Repaint & Signal-Hygiene Idioms
// Extracted 2026-07-22 from patterns in live use across every
// engine this project ships. Status: in-use, not formally
// cross-asset validated. NOT a standalone indicator.
// ============================================================

// §1 — ta.* calls run UNCONDITIONALLY at top level (BUG-004).
// Cross/stateful functions (ta.crossover, ta.rsi, ta.barssince...)
// nested inside `if` blocks miss bars and corrupt their state.
// Pattern: compute every series every bar; gate only the ACTION:
//
// bool crossed = ta.crossover(a, b)   // top level, every bar
// if enabled and crossed
//     doThing()

// §2 — HTF references, non-repainting idiom used repo-wide:
// prior-period values with lookahead_on = a FIXED, already-closed
// value that never changes intrabar:
//
// prevDayHigh = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", high[1],
//      lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
//
// (high[1] + lookahead_on = yesterday's completed high, static all
// day. lookahead_on with a NON-offset series would be lookahead
// bias -- the [1] is what makes this safe.)

// §3 — Cooldown + price-distance re-arm state machine (BUG-006).
// Bar-count cooldown alone lets a static level re-fire; identity-
// change checks are trivially true. Gate on price distance ALONE:
//
// var int   lastSigBar   = -9999
// var float lastSigPrice = na
// bool cd    = bar_index - lastSigBar > cooldownBars
// bool rearm = na(lastSigPrice) or math.abs(close - lastSigPrice) >= atr * minReArmAtr
// if signal and cd and rearm
//     lastSigBar := bar_index
//     lastSigPrice := close

// §4 — Hit-tracking never checks the entry bar (standard tracker):
// if trkActive and bar_index > trkBar
//     ... stop/target checks ...
// (same-bar checks let the entry candle's own range fake a fill)
